            "created_at": "2025-09-19T19:32:34.375764+00:00",
            "notes": "### Powers\n\n[Chain Grasp](item_17b85f3e-1b10-410d-8e02-c7ff61f502a0) is typically the best choice as a first power, but there are times when you may choose [Ethereal Excision](item_a2359da3-1aa5-406f-a82f-4a0bd66266ac) or [Phantasm](item_21ed9c3d-7a54-438f-9188-f21fd7a7dbfb). If they are running poke heroes, they often won't be near [D.Va](hero_e8e1dc68-45c4-47c2-b421-95e33594e6b6), and your goal is to generate as much cash as possible, so consider one of the other powers. With Chain Grasp, fire [Biotic Orb](ability_721997d0-c151-4a4c-bb11-86552b14def6)s at alternate angles and away from or behind D.Va. I usually fire healing orbs into my team, or at the ground/ceiling in an enclosed space, and proc Chain Grasp that way. \n\nPhantasm is my favorite Moira power, so I try to make it work in any build. Against D.Va, it's helpful if you have a dive-heavy team or the enemy team has squishies you can pick on. If you choose Phantasm, also take [Power Playbook](item_6d8803cf-baa7-46ee-af91-51e7f2301418), and strategically place stationary healing orbs behind walls or around corners so D.Va doesn't eat them. When I go this route, I often focus on [Ability Power](stat_ability_power) and tailor my build for harassing the enemy backline in the later rounds. With this build, I mostly stay behind cover and [Fade](ability_438ee61f-f7ed-4321-9ca3-d3577b89ba19) off cool down to keep placing healing orbs near my team to generate cash.\n\nIf the enemy team has flyers or highly mobile heroes, Ethereal Excision gives you extra sustain and focuses on single-target damage. For example, if they have D.Va, [Pharah](hero_0baf7420-ff13-4b92-81f7-ca21b61dacf9), [Freja](hero_e80840a1-845d-4008-966c-585b7cb4a424), [Mercy](hero_0e213bfc-3ca9-49c6-9036-e7f344b752da), and [Moira](hero_7fb6ff1e-a193-40c0-bd0a-25c1928fbaed), you won't get as much out of Chain Grasp, so taking Ethereal Excision is a solid alternative.\n\n### Items\n\nIf I'm more likely to be in a brawl or otherwise require more sustain, I'll choose [Armored Vest](item_358361e2-59be-4c81-b221-8a87f37809e6) as the $1500 item. If I'm mostly hanging around my team and dropping stationary orbs or behind cover, [First Aid Kit](item_0172eaaa-1902-44a3-b989-d12f0f7301da) is a good choice to maintain uptime. \n\n[Frenzy Amplifier](item_d4b0cfcb-14e9-4472-a688-680120217250) can be useful if the enemy team has a [Kiriko](hero_70a0ac5c-2a55-4fab-beeb-2f570886426f) and chooses [Clone Conjuration](item_6c9f6be1-ab29-4f46-af24-34e4835f9af3) because combining it with Chain Grasp kills the clones and procs Frenzy Amplifier. It's a bit of a gamble, but it can give you a pretty significant cash boost if Kiriko is running clones.\n\n[Weapon Grease](item_961ae72f-434f-406b-a89b-ab8efec806bf) and [Compensator](item_2a354f80-610c-4661-9bdd-8960ae1a60b0) are filler items if you don't choose the other options.",
